=== Wear OS System Service Privilege Escalation Hunt ===
Date: 2026-09-11
Target: Pixel Watch 2 (3A101RTJWRGCV9, eos, CP2A.260603.001, Android 17, SDK 37)

OBJECTIVE: Find createPackageContext(CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE | CONTEXT_IGNORE_SECURITY) patterns
similar to CVE-2026-49881 (InCallController.serviceClassExists) in other system services.

=== METHODOLOGY ===
Decompiled and searched ALL of these for createPackageContext with INCLUDE_CODE:
- /system/framework/services.jar (17.5MB, 4917 classes) — main system_server
- /system/framework/wear-service.jar (1.6MB, 726 classes) — Wear service APIs
- /system/framework/clockwork-system.jar (262KB, 65 classes)
- /system/framework/clockwork-ambient.jar (458KB, 79 classes)
- /system/framework/clockwork-healthservices.jar (115KB, 25 classes)
- /apex/com.android.telephonycore/javalib/service-telecom.jar (1.8MB) — CONFIRMED VULN
- /apex/com.android.bt/javalib/service-bluetooth.jar (549KB, 301 classes)
- /apex/com.android.wifi/javalib/service-wifi.jar (5.5MB, 933 classes)

=== RESULTS ===

CONFIRMED VULNERABLE:
1. InCallController.serviceClassExists() in service-telecom.jar
   - Line 2261: createPackageContextAsUser(serviceInfo.packageName, 3, userHandle)
   - Flag 3 = CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE | CONTEXT_IGNORE_SECURITY
   - EXPLOITED: Achieved UID 1000 system_server code execution

NO OTHER INSTANCE OF CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE IN ANY SYSTEM SERVICE JAR:
- services.jar: 30+ createPackageContextAsUser calls, ALL use flag 0
- wear-service.jar: 1 createPackageContext call, uses flag 0
- clockwork-system.jar: No createPackageContext calls
- clockwork-ambient.jar: No createPackageContext calls
- clockwork-healthservices.jar: No createPackageContext calls
- service-bluetooth.jar: 1 createPackageContextAsUser, flag 0
- service-wifi.jar: 4 createPackageContextAsUser calls, ALL flag 0

=== SECONDARY ANALYSIS: Service Binding Patterns ===
Checked system services that bind to user-declared components:
- DreamController: bindServiceAsUser to dream services (normal binding, no code loading)
- WallpaperManagerService: bindService to wallpaper services (normal binding)
- CompanionDeviceManager: No direct bindService in decompiled code
- WatchFaceManager: bindService only to com.google.android.apps.wearable.systemui (hardcoded)
- HandlerBindingAgent: bindService only to hardcoded WHS component
- SystemUiApiProxy: bindService only to SystemUI (hardcoded)
- AppFunctionManagerService: bindService + unbindService, createPackageContext flag 0

=== WEAR-SPECIFIC SERVICES CHECKED ===
328 total system services on device. Wear-specific:
- wear_service (IWear) — runs in system_server, hardcoded bindings only
- HealthService (IHealthService) — binds to hardcoded WHS component
- DisplayOffloadService — no untrusted code loading
- WearConnectivityService — no createPackageContext
- WearPowerService — no code loading patterns
- ModeManager — mode management only
- companiondevice — no INCLUDE_CODE usage

=== CONCLUSION ===
The InCallController.serviceClassExists() vulnerability (CVE-2026-49881) is UNIQUE in that it
is the ONLY instance across ALL analyzed system service JARs on the Pixel Watch 2 that uses
createPackageContext with CONTEXT_INCLUDE_CODE on an untrusted package name. This is likely
why it wasn't caught during earlier code reviews — the pattern is extremely rare in Android
system services.

No other similar privilege escalation path found via createPackageContext code loading in the
Wear OS system services. The InCallController vulnerability on this watch is confirmed and
exploited as UID 1000 system_server.
